# Security Rules

## Secrets Management

- API keys, secrets, and tokens go ONLY in `.env` — never in code, config.yaml, or comments
- `.env` is in `.gitignore` — never committed
- Use `.env.example` with placeholder values as a template
- Load secrets via `python-dotenv` or Pydantic Settings

## Binance API Key Permissions

- Enable ONLY: "Read Info" + "Spot Trading"
- NEVER enable "Enable Withdrawals"
- Set IP whitelist to the server/machine running the bot
- Enable 2FA on the Binance account

## Anthropic API Key

- Separate from exchange keys — different rotation schedule
- Track usage/costs via logging (token counts per call)

## Code Rules

- Never log API keys, even partially
- Never include secrets in error messages or exception strings
- Validate that required env vars exist at startup — fail fast with clear message
- Paper trading mode must work without any exchange API key (uses public endpoints only)

## Live Trading Safeguards

- Two-stage verification before executing live trades: strategy signal + risk manager approval
- Log every live order with full context before execution
- Maximum single order size limit as hard cap in config
- Kill switch: ability to halt all trading immediately via API endpoint
